   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to expanding the\nresidential parking permit system within the area known as Elmont in the town\nof Hempstead",
    "basePrintNo": "S6627",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6627-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1662-e, V & T L",
    "lawSection": "Vehicle and Traffic Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S6627\n\nSPONSOR: CANZONERI-FITZPATRICK\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the vehicle and traffic law, in relation to expanding\nthe residential parking permit system within the area known as Elmont in\nthe town of Hempstead\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo expand the resident parking permit system in Elmont in the Town of\nHempstead.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends Section 1662-e of the Vehicle and Traffic Law to\nexpand the residential parking permit system in Elmont in the Town of\nHempstead to include all of Sussex Road.\n\nSection 2: Provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nResidents and members of local civic associations have expressed\nconcerns regarding the availability of parking for residents in the area\nof Elmont in the Town of Hempstead. This legislation would alleviate\nthis issue by permitting the Town of Hempstead to expand the existing\nresident parking district to include all of Sussex Road, which is\ncurrently limited to only the portion of Sussex Road north of 109th\nAvenue.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
